<div class="box tabular settings">
  <h3>Bell Notifications Settings</h3>

  <p>
    <label for="settings_dropdown_limit">Notifications in dropdown</label>
    <%= number_field_tag 'settings[dropdown_limit]',
                         @settings['dropdown_limit'] || 10,
                         min: 5,
                         max: 50,
                         class: 'small' %>
    <em class="info">Number of notifications to display in the dropdown (5-50). Default: 10</em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <label for="settings_retention_days">Retention period (days)</label>
    <%= number_field_tag 'settings[retention_days]',
                         @settings['retention_days'] || 180,
                         min: 30,
                         max: 365,
                         class: 'small' %>
    <em class="info">How long to keep notifications before automatic cleanup (30-365 days). Default: 180 days (6 months)</em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <label for="settings_cleanup_interval">Cleanup interval (hours)</label>
    <%= number_field_tag 'settings[cleanup_interval]',
                         @settings['cleanup_interval'] || 24,
                         min: 1,
                         max: 168,
                         class: 'small' %>
    <em class="info">How often to run automatic cleanup (1-168 hours). Default: 24 hours (once per day)</em>
  </p>

  <p class="info">
    <strong>Automatic Cleanup:</strong> The plugin automatically cleans up old notifications in the background.
    Cleanup runs every <%= @settings['cleanup_interval'] || 24 %> hours and deletes notifications older than <%= @settings['retention_days'] || 180 %> days.
    <strong>No cron job required!</strong>
  </p>

  <p class="info">
    <strong>Note:</strong> Bell notifications work independently of email settings.
    Even if email delivery is disabled, in-app notifications will still be created.
  </p>

  <p class="info">
    <strong>Manual Cleanup:</strong> You can also manually run <code>rake redmine:bell_notifications:cleanup RAILS_ENV=production</code>
    to trigger cleanup immediately.
  </p>
</div>
